  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The investigation into Kupang Regent Yosef Lede regarding allegations of sexual assault remains ongoing under the direction of the East Nusa Tenggara (NTT) Regional Police. Authorities have gathered various pieces of evidence, including forensic examination results and clothing worn by the complainant, a university student. Law enforcement has been systematically questioning witnesses, including local Satpol PP officers and individuals who allegedly facilitated the meeting between the victim and the regent. While police have prepared to interrogate the regent, his legal team reportedly requested a rescheduling of the examination. The case has drawn significant attention from national officials, with calls for a swift and uncompromising investigation into the alleged sexual violence. Representatives from the Ministry of Women Empowerment and Child Protection have emphasized that no settlement outside of the legal process should be considered for such grave allegations.",
